(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-12-22","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: During a DFPS investigation it was determined that although the operation had a procedure in place to properly account for all children in care, it was not followed by two caregivers resulting in a child being left in an attached breezeway outside the day care for approximately eight minutes.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026553645","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20231103-2-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20231103-2","date":"2023-11-03","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-12-22","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: During a DFPS investigation, it was determined that caregivers failed to properly supervise a child in their care, and did not account for child when returning indoors resulting in child being left outside in a breezeway that is attached to the daycare for approximately eight minutes.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026553644","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20231103-2-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20231103-2","date":"2023-11-03","original_code":"746.1201(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":