trieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2023-01-25","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20230125-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20230125","date":"2023-01-25","original_code":"746.5202(3)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-02-03","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Essential Documentation: The operations emergency preparedness plan was missing specific procedures on the following topics:  How staff will evacuate and relocate with the essential documentation including (A)Parent and emergency contact telephone numbers for each child in care, (B) Authorization for emergency care for each child in care & (C) The child tracking system information for children in care","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026227062","violation_type_title":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Essential Documentation (26 TAC §746.5202(3))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20230125-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-4751-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20230125","date":"2023-01-25","original_code":"746.4751(b)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Maintenance Procedures for Active Play - Monthly Maintenance Checklist: There were no monthly inspections of the active play space and equipment, utilizing a general maintenance checklist or safety checklist documented for the last calender year.     Note: This was corrected during the inspection when the director conducted an inspection utilizing From 1100 - Daily Building and Grounds Checklist.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026307279","violation_type_title":"Maintenance Procedures for Active Play - Monthly Maintenance Checklist (26 TAC §746.4751(b))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20230125-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3819","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20230125","date":"2023-01-25","original_code":"746.3819","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-02-27","finding":"Food Allergy Emergency Plan Signed by Parents and Health Care Professional: A childs food allergy emergency plan was not signed or dated by the child's parents.","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026387829","violation_type_title":"Food Allergy Emergency Plan Signed by Parents and Health Care Professional (26 TAC §746.3819)","topic_label":"Fire safety & emergency drills"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20230125-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20230125","date":"2023-01-25","original_code":"746.5202(1)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-02-03","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Evacuation, relocation, and sheltering/lock-down procedures: The operations emergency preparedness plan was missing  specific procedures on the following topics:  (1) How children will be evacuated or relocated to the designated safe area or alternate shelter, including specific procedures for evacuating and relocating children who are under 24 months of age, who have limited mobility, or who otherwise may need assistance in an emergency, such as children who have mental, visual, or hearing impairments, (2) An emergency evacuation and relocation diagram & (3) How children in attendance at the time of the emergency will be accounted for at the designated safe area or alternate shelter.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026467895","violation_type_title":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Evacuation, relocation, and sheltering/lock-down procedures (26 TAC §746.5202(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-97569-i20230125-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","inspection_id":"tx-hh